5)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 85 people. Revenue per employee of $10.9M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $167K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["NNN REIT, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $8.0B market cap on $926M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 2.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.016829416015989737},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 41% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","35 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"$500,000 in Realty Income and NNN REIT: How Much More You Keep in a Roth IRA","source":"247wallst.com","link":"https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/11/13/500000-in-realty-income-and-nnn-reit-how-much-more-you-keep-in-a-roth-ira/","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794597453.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.637,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"AQR Capital Reports 4.68% Ownership Stake in NNN REIT, Inc.","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/aqr-capital-reports-468-ownership-stake-in-nnn-reit-inc","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794502974.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Did Earnings Growth Just Shift NNN REIT's (NNN) Investment Narrative?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-nnn/nnn-reit/news/did-earnings-growth-just-shift-nnn-reits-nnn-investment-narr","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794471984.751,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.637,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"